    turnFlow: 'Deal thirteen cards to each player. The leader plays a single card or a matching set, optionally completed with wild cards. Later players may pass or play the same number of cards at a higher rank. When everyone passes, the last successful raiser clears the table and leads the next combination. Play continues until players empty their hands and receive ranks.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Big Two is a point-based shedding game played without a pre-hand monetary ante.',
      deal: 'The entire 52-card deck is distributed equally by the system dealer at the start of the round.',
